==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-end up.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive|or|intransitive|copulative}} To [[conclude]], [[turn out]], sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''That's just how things '''ended up''' happening.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[arrive]] at a destination, sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''I was going for a stroll, and '''ended up''' lost.''
# {{lb|en|of a set of events}} To [[eventually]] [[do]]
#: ''We spent a long time looking for a cheaper deal, but we '''ended up''' buying from the first dealer we met.''
# To lift or tilt, so as to set on end.
#: ''to '''end up''' a hogshead''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|turn out}} {{l|en|conclude}}, {{l|en|end}}, {{l|en|turn out}}
* {{sense|arrive at a destination}} {{l|en|finish up}}, {{l|en|wind up}}

